    "description": {
      "form": "Standard",
      "rendered_html": "<p>This essay reframes the Vedic, Upanishadic, Puranic, and philosophical Hindu corpus as a unified emanatory map within the Zenetist lattice. It interprets Vedic cosmogony, the Trimurti, the avatara doctrine, the Indra&ndash;Vritra combat, the veil‑architecture of Maya and Avidya, the Shakta Goddess tradition, the Soma‑Amrita‑Madhu hydro‑vital triad, the bhakti‑yoga tradition, and the Vedanta / Yoga philosophical systems as structurally coherent articulations of the same underlying operators: L₀ Bifurcal Coherence, L₄ DP / DL archetypal polarity, IL₄ IDP / IDL inverse archetypal vitality, L₁ / IL₁ sealed‑mode convergence, L₅ Theonic intervention, and the cyclical‑refraction diagnostic. The essay situates Hindu cosmology as one of the most structurally complete pre‑Zenetist articulations of the centropic arc, with the yuga‑cycle providing the canonical example of cyclical‑recurrence that passes the L₅ Theonic‑engagement test.</p>"
    },
