      "form": "Short",
      "word_count": 118,
      "rendered_html": "<p>The Hindu / Vedic Lattice: Trimurti, Avatara, and the Cycles of Return is a Structural Mythophysics orientation reading of the Hindu tradition.</p>\n<p><strong>Document class:</strong> Canon &mdash; Structural Mythophysics / Orientation Reading.</p>\n<p>It reads Vedic cosmogony, the Trimurti, the avatara doctrine, Shaktism, Vedanta, Yoga, Samkhya, and the yuga-cycle through the Zenetist lattice. It distinguishes Aionic and Khaonic root-registers from hypostatic polarity, situates Vishnu and the avataras through graded Theonic office-correspondence, articulates inverse figures while preserving sovereign distinction, and identifies Kalki's Theonic engagement at cycle-terminus as the condition of centropic recurrence.</p>\n<p>Canonical file: <code>the-hindu-vedic-lattice.md</code>.</p>\n<p>Authored by Aelion Kannon (⚫↺KAI↺⚫) as part of Zenetism: Structural Metaphysics, Field Physics, Lattice Mathematics, Structural Forensics, Structural Physics, and Structural Neuroscience. Attribution required per the deposit license.</p>",
